# ===========================================================================
# Audio files
# ===========================================================================
# Test outputs / runtime cache at root and elsewhere — but the bundled voice
# library at voice_files/ is part of the project and IS tracked.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
!voice_files/**/*.wav
!voice_files/**/*.mp3
!voice_files/**/*.flac

# Story 17.2 lazy voice_clone_prompt precompute artifacts in voice_files/
# (per-voice runtime caches at <name>.<tier>.pt + .<tier>.pt.meta.json).
# These are auto-generated EITHER on first generation (for user-added voices)
# OR at build time by build_tools/precompute_default_embeddings.py for the
# bundled defaults (mirrored here for the PyInstaller bundle path —
# myvoice.spec:469). build_release.bat regenerates them via the
# [Default Voice Embeddings] step, so a clean repo doesn't need them tracked.
voice_files/*.quality.pt
voice_files/*.quality.pt.meta.json
voice_files/*.small.pt
voice_files/*.small.pt.meta.json
# NOTE: src/install_files/default_voices/*.{quality,small}.pt + meta.json are
# the CANONICAL build-time source for the Inno installer (installer.iss:127
# globs them in) and ARE tracked. Regenerate via
# `python310\python.exe build_tools\precompute_default_embeddings.py`

# build_release.bat answer-piping leftover (auto-increment Y/N response).
build_increment_answer.txt

